{
  "uid": "wasm-bench-health",
  "title": "wasm bench: measurement health",
  "description": "Whether this run's numbers can be trusted. Client saturation has produced a confident wrong answer in this harness before (METHODOLOGY 29) and nothing broker-side revealed it, so the client host panels come first.",
  "tags": [
    "wasm-bench"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {
    "refresh_intervals": [
      "2s",
      "5s",
      "10s",
      "30s",
      "1m",
      "5m"
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Client hosts - client0 is loadgen and must have headroom",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU utilisation by host",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "1 - avg by (host) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\",role=\"client\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "client0 runs loadgen and nothing else, deliberately, so that pacing stays clean. client1 is the external matcher. client2 and up carry the background consumer groups at ~84 each. If client0 is near saturation, the measurement is of a starved load generator and not of the architecture - see METHODOLOGY 29, which is exactly this failure.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "run-queue pressure by host (load / cores)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (host) (node_load1{role=\"client\"}) / count by (host) (node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\",role=\"client\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Load average normalised by core count, so 1.0 means the run queue is as long as the machine is wide. Catches a client that is not CPU-pegged but is still waiting to be scheduled, which is what a paced generator is most sensitive to.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Broker hosts",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU utilisation by broker",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "1 - avg by (host) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\",role=\"broker\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Whole-host CPU, so it covers the 19 vCPU redpanda is not using as well as its own 13. Compare against the per-shard reactor panel on the overview: a busy shard with an idle host is a placement result, not a capacity one.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "network in/out by broker",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (host) (rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{role=\"broker\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 8",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} in",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (host) (rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{role=\"broker\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 8",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} out",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "The external arm's fan-out is paid here, as egress to 500 consumers. The in-broker arm's is not, which is most of the point of the comparison.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "transform bytes in/out",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_transform_read_bytes[$__rate_interval])) * 8",
          "legendFormat": "read",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_transform_write_bytes[$__rate_interval])) * 8",
          "legendFormat": "written",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "loadgen live metrics (only up while a window is running)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "send lateness against the pacing interval",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(loadgen_send_lateness_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(loadgen_send_lateness_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(loadgen_send_lateness_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "How late each produce call was against its scheduled slot. At RATE=1000 the pacing interval is 1,000us, so a p99 approaching that means the generator is no longer holding the offered rate and its latency figures include its own queueing. This is the single most useful client-side number in the harness. Needs loadgen started with -metrics-listen; empty otherwise.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "offered vs acknowledged rate",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(loadgen_orders_sent_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "orders sent/s",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(loadgen_orders_acked_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "orders acked/s",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(loadgen_receipts_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "receipts/s",
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Sent tracking acked tracking receipts is a healthy window. Sent above acked means the broker is applying backpressure; receipts below acked means output is not coming back, which the run's own `missing` count will also report.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The observer itself",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "prometheus scrape duration by job",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max by (job) (scrape_duration_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "If a scrape duration approaches its interval, Prometheus is the bottleneck and the gaps in these panels are its fault rather than the cluster's. redpanda-internal is expected to be the slow one; it is scraped at 15s for that reason.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "targets up by job",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (job) (up)",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "loadgen is expected to be down between runs - it is a batch process, not a service. Everything else should be flat at its instance count for the whole run.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  }
}
